        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "646fd60f-24be-5f7a-b3f3-4124f5bbaff8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Vanessa; Le roi malgré lui\n- People: Samuel Barber; Gian-Carlo Menotti; Emmanuel Chabrier; Emile de Najac; Paul Burani; Nicolai Gedda\n- Organizations: Metropolitan Opera\n- Roles: Anatol\n\nFacts:\n- In 1887, Emmanuel Chabrier's Le roi malgré lui was composed as an opéra-comique in three acts with an original libretto by Emile de Najac and Paul Burani.\n- Samuel Barber's Vanessa is an American opera in three acts, originally four acts, and is opus 32.\n- Gian-Carlo Menotti wrote the original English libretto for Samuel Barber's Vanessa.\n- In January 1958, Nicolai Gedda created the role of Anatol in the world premiere of Samuel Barber's Vanessa at the Metropolitan Opera.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "04a2ad8a-d85f-5a5d-ab2e-6695b3c7655b",
        "text": "Page: Vanessa (opera). Sentence: Vanessa is an American opera in three (originally four) acts by Samuel Barber, opus 32, with an original English libretto by Gian-Carlo Menotti.\nPage: Le roi malgré lui. Sentence: Le roi malgré lui (\"King in Spite of Himself\" or \"The reluctant king\") is an opéra-comique in three acts by Emmanuel Chabrier of 1887 with an original libretto by Emile de Najac and Paul Burani.\nPage: Nicolai Gedda. Sentence: In January 1958, he created the part of Anatol in the world premiere of the American opera \"Vanessa\" at the Metropolitan Opera.",
